# Discovery to numeric proposal to one explicit simulated effect

## Goal

Run the canonical smart room end to end: discover Things from an explicit
Directory by their own TD ids, consume an HTTP thermostat, an MQTT energy
meter and a loopback actuator through the runtime, exchange observation
proposals over the Continuum channel, infer a `setTarget` proposal with a
small `defn`, let the policy grant one decision, dispatch it exactly once at
the edge, read the effect back from the actuator, and let only the
`action_result` cross to the cloud host. Every step is a separate,
inspectable record, and a second dispatch of the same decision is refused.

## Prerequisites

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:wotex_lab, "~> 0.1.0"},
  {:nx, "~> 0.13.1"},
  {:req, "~> 0.7.4"},
  {:emqtt, "~> 1.15", system_env: [{"BUILD_WITHOUT_QUIC", "1"}]},
  {:bandit, "~> 1.12"},
  {:plug, "~> 1.18"}
])
```

The requirements above are published-artifact requirements. At the time this
notebook was written none of the `wotex*` packages is published on Hex; the
notebook is verified against the workspace source cohort recorded in
`priv/provenance/source-cohort.json` by `test/wotex/lab/cookbook_test.exs`,
which evaluates every Elixir cell below in order (skipping this install
cell). `Mix.install/1` never points at a Git checkout.

The thermostat is a Bandit server started here. The energy meter needs an
MQTT peer: inside the Lab checkout the scripted in-BEAM peer from
`test/support/mqtt_server.ex` serves a retained `2500` W reading; outside
it, bind `broker_href` or set `WOTEX_LAB_MQTT_HREF` to a broker you run and
the notebook seeds the retained reading itself. Without either, the room
runs without a meter and the meter check is omitted.

## Package and consumer ownership

| Concern | Owner | Where |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Directory listing and entries | `wotex_directory` | `Wotex.Directory.list/3` |
| Consumed Things, requests, results | `wotex_runtime` | `Wotex.Runtime.ConsumedThing` |
| HTTP and MQTT values and mappings | `wotex_binding_http`, `wotex_binding_mqtt` | the two bindings |
| Rows, batches, decoded proposals | `wotex_nx` | `Wotex.Nx.Encoder`, `Decoder` |
| Continuum values and codec | `wotex_continuum` | `WotexContinuum.Codec` |
| Discovery, inference, the room rule, exchange, dispatch order | `wotex_lab` (consumer) | `Wotex.Lab.SmartRoom.Scenario` |
| Authority: grant, refuse, dispatch once | `wotex_lab` (consumer) | `Wotex.Lab.SmartRoom.Policy` |
| Nx effects | none: the proposal is inert until the policy dispatches it | `Policy.dispatch/4` |
| Servers, peers, stores and their lifetimes | this notebook | below |

## Run

```elixir
alias Wotex.Binding.HTTP
alias Wotex.Binding.MQTT
alias Wotex.Binding.MQTT.{Broker, Command, Transport, TransportConfig}
alias Wotex.Directory
alias Wotex.Directory.{Context, Service}
alias Wotex.Lab
alias Wotex.Lab.Adapters.Directory.{Authorization, Clock, EtsRepository, Identifier}
alias Wotex.Lab.Adapters.HTTP.ReqClient
alias Wotex.Lab.Adapters.MQTT.EmqttClient
alias Wotex.Lab.Adapters.Runtime.{Loopback, StaticRef}
alias Wotex.Lab.Continuum.{Channel, Host}
alias Wotex.Lab.Error, as: LabError
alias Wotex.Lab.Reference.Thing
alias Wotex.Lab.SmartRoom.{Policy, Scenario}
alias Wotex.Lab.Telemetry
alias Wotex.Nx.{ActionProposal, Observation}
alias Wotex.Runtime.{BindingProfile, Result}
alias Wotex.Runtime.Context, as: RuntimeContext
alias Wotex.Runtime.ExecutionContext
alias Wotex.ThingDescription
alias WotexContinuum.{Capability, Codec}

telemetry_id = "cookbook-smart-room-#{System.unique_integer([:positive])}"

events =
  for component <- Telemetry.components(),
      operation <- Telemetry.operations(),
      event <- [:start, :stop, :exception],
      do: [:wotex, :lab, component, operation, event]

:ok = :telemetry.attach_many(telemetry_id, events, &Telemetry.forward/4, self())
epoch = ~U[2026-09-08 12:00:00Z]
token = "room-token-7f3a"
```

The thermostat: one HTTP Property, served by a per-run function plug without
compiling a shared module when another notebook evaluation is active.

```elixir
import Plug.Conn

http_handler = fn conn, _options ->
  case {conn.method, conn.request_path} do
    {"GET", "/properties/temperature"} ->
      conn |> put_resp_content_type("application/json") |> send_resp(200, "21.5")

    _other ->
      send_resp(conn, 404, "")
  end
end

{:ok, server} =
  Bandit.start_link(plug: http_handler, ip: {127, 0, 0, 1}, port: 0, startup_log: false)

{:ok, {_ip, port}} = ThousandIsland.listener_info(server)

{:ok, thermostat_td} =
  ThingDescription.from_map(%{
    "@context" => Wotex.td_context_1_1(),
    "id" => "urn:wotex:lab:http:room",
    "title" => "HTTP thermostat",
    "base" => "http://127.0.0.1:#{port}/",
    "security" => ["nosec_sc"],
    "securityDefinitions" => %{"nosec_sc" => %{"scheme" => "nosec"}},
    "properties" => %{
      "temperature" => %{
        "type" => "number",
        "unit" => "Cel",
        "forms" => [%{"href" => "properties/temperature", "contentType" => "application/json", "op" => "readproperty"}]
      }
    }
  })

ThingDescription.id(thermostat_td)
```

The energy meter: a retained `power` reading on an MQTT peer, when one is
available.

```elixir
broker_href = Keyword.get(binding(), :broker_href) || System.get_env("WOTEX_LAB_MQTT_HREF")
scripted? = Code.ensure_loaded?(Wotex.Lab.Test.MqttServer) and broker_href == nil
meter_prefix = "lab/cookbook/meter/#{System.unique_integer([:positive])}"
power_topic = "#{meter_prefix}/properties/power"

peer =
  if scripted?,
    do: Wotex.Lab.Test.MqttServer.start(self(), retained: {power_topic, "2500"}, on_exit: false),
    else: nil

meter_href =
  cond do
    scripted? -> Wotex.Lab.Test.MqttServer.href(peer)
    is_binary(broker_href) -> broker_href
    true -> nil
  end

if meter_href != nil and not scripted? do
  {:ok, broker} = Broker.new(meter_href)
  {:ok, seed} = Command.publish(broker, :writeproperty, power_topic, 2500, qos: 1, retain: true)
  execution_context = ExecutionContext.new(RuntimeContext.new!(request_id: "meter-seed"), nil)
  :ok = EmqttClient.publish(seed, execution_context, %{connect_timeout: 2_000})
end

meter_td =
  if meter_href do
    {:ok, td} =
      ThingDescription.from_map(%{
        "@context" => Wotex.td_context_1_1(),
        "id" => "urn:wotex:lab:mqtt:meter",
        "title" => "MQTT energy meter",
        "security" => ["nosec_sc"],
        "securityDefinitions" => %{"nosec_sc" => %{"scheme" => "nosec"}},
        "properties" => %{
          "power" => %{
            "type" => "number",
            "unit" => "W",
            "forms" => [
              %{
                "href" => meter_href,
                "contentType" => "application/json",
                "op" => "readproperty",
                "mqv:filter" => power_topic,
                "mqv:retain" => true,
                "mqv:qos" => 1
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      })

    td
  end

{scripted?, meter_td != nil}
```

The actuator is the loopback fixture Thing with an explicit `setTarget`
effect. The Directory holds every TD; discovery pages through it and builds a
`ConsumedThing` per TD id with the caller's profiles, transports and
credential port.

```elixir
{:ok, lab} = Lab.start_link(id: "smart-room", max_children: 32)
{:ok, actuator_td} = Application.app_dir(:wotex_lab, "priv/fixtures/loopback/thing-description.json") |> File.read!() |> ThingDescription.parse()

{:ok, actuator} =
  Lab.start_child(
    lab,
    :things,
    {Thing,
     td: actuator_td,
     state: %{"temperature" => 20.0, "target" => 21.0},
     tokens: %{"bearer_sc" => token},
     actions: %{
       "setTarget" => fn input, state -> {:ok, %{"accepted" => true}, :accepted, Map.put(state, "target", input)} end
     }}
  )

{:ok, repository} = Lab.start_child(lab, :things, {EtsRepository, id: :directory})
{:ok, clock} = Clock.start_link(epoch)
{:ok, identifier} = Identifier.start_link()

{:ok, service} =
  Service.new(
    repository: {EtsRepository, repository},
    authorization: {Authorization, :allow_all},
    clock: {Clock, {:agent, clock}},
    identifier: {Identifier, identifier},
    introduction: thermostat_td
  )

directory_context = Context.new!(:operator)
{:ok, _thermostat} = Directory.register(service, thermostat_td, directory_context)
{:ok, _actuator} = Directory.register(service, actuator_td, directory_context)
if meter_td, do: {:ok, _meter} = Directory.register(service, meter_td, directory_context)

{:ok, http_profile} = HTTP.profile()
{:ok, http_config} = HTTP.config(client: {ReqClient, %{}})
{:ok, mqtt_config} = TransportConfig.new(EmqttClient, %{connect_timeout: 2_000}, read_timeout: 5_000)
{:ok, loopback_profile} = BindingProfile.new(id: :loopback, schemes: ["loopback"], operations: Wotex.Runtime.operations())

transport_opts = [
  profiles: [http_profile, loopback_profile, MQTT.profile()],
  transports: %{
    http_profile.id => HTTP.transport(http_config),
    loopback: {Loopback, %{host: actuator}},
    mqtt: {Transport, mqtt_config}
  },
  credentials: {StaticRef, %{references: %{"bearer_sc" => "ref"}, lookup: fn "ref" -> {:ok, token} end}}
]

{:ok, things} = Scenario.discover(service, directory_context, transport_opts)
Map.keys(things) |> Enum.sort()
```

The exchange and the authority: a channel to a cloud host that has admitted
a manifest, and a policy that allows the `:operator` principal to set targets
between 5 and 35 degrees.

```elixir
{:ok, capability} =
  Capability.from_map(%{
    id: "observation-forwarding",
    version: "2.1.0",
    operations: ["forward"],
    modes: [:hybrid, :saas],
    network: :external,
    degradation: :queue
  })

{:ok, manifest} =
  Application.app_dir(:wotex_lab, "priv/fixtures/continuum/continuum-manifest.json") |> File.read!() |> Codec.decode()

{:ok, channel} = Lab.start_child(lab, :sessions, {Channel, id: :room_channel, clock: fn -> epoch end, capacity: 32})

{:ok, host} =
  Lab.start_child(
    lab,
    :sessions,
    {Host, id: :room_host, channel: channel, endpoint: "cloud", clock: fn -> epoch end, things: things, capabilities: [capability]}
  )

:ok = Channel.attach(channel, "edge", self())
{:ok, _manifest} = Channel.send_value(channel, "edge", "cloud", manifest)

{:ok, policy} =
  Lab.start_child(lab, :sessions, {Policy, id: :policy, allowed: [:operator], limits: %{"setTarget" => %{min: 5, max: 35}}})

run_opts = [
  things: things,
  thermostat_id: ThingDescription.id(thermostat_td),
  actuator_id: ThingDescription.id(actuator_td),
  meter_id: nil,
  channel: channel,
  edge: "edge",
  cloud: "cloud",
  policy: policy,
  principal: :operator,
  now: 1_000,
  epoch: epoch,
  scope: Scenario.scope("edge", epoch),
  watermark: 1,
  state_revision: 1
]

wait_until = fn read, predicate ->
  Enum.reduce_while(1..200, read.(), fn _attempt, value ->
    if predicate.(value), do: {:halt, value}, else: (Process.sleep(5) && {:cont, read.()})
  end)
end

:ok
```

One control cycle without the meter: `21.5` observed, the comfort rule
proposes `22.5`, the policy grants, the actuator is set once, and the cloud
host received the manifest, the proposal and the result.

```elixir
{:ok, run} = Scenario.run(run_opts)
proposal_fields = ActionProposal.to_map(run.action_proposal)
{:ok, %Result{status: dispatch_status}} = run.dispatch
stats = wait_until.(fn -> Host.stats(host) end, &(length(&1.received) == 3))
actuator_after_run = Thing.stats(actuator)

%{
  proposal: {proposal_fields.action_name, proposal_fields.input},
  decision: {run.decision.status, run.decision.proposal_digest == Policy.proposal_digest(run.action_proposal)},
  dispatch: dispatch_status,
  effect: run.effect,
  actuator: actuator_after_run,
  cloud_received: Enum.map(stats.received, & &1.kind),
  cloud_observations: stats.observations
}
```

With the meter over budget, the rule lowers the target instead; with a
higher budget it raises it again.

```elixir
meter_runs =
  if meter_td do
    meter_id = ThingDescription.id(meter_td)
    {:ok, over} = Scenario.run(Keyword.merge(run_opts, meter_id: meter_id, now: 2_000, watermark: 2))
    {:ok, under} = Scenario.run(Keyword.merge(run_opts, meter_id: meter_id, now: 3_000, watermark: 3, power_budget: 3_000.0))
    %{power: Observation.to_map(over.power_observation).value, over_effect: over.effect, under_effect: under.effect}
  else
    :no_meter
  end
```

## Deliberate breakage

The same decision cannot dispatch twice; a proposal for an undiscovered
Thing is a typed scenario error; and a stranger, an expired grant and a
stale watermark dispatch nothing.

```elixir
{:error, %LabError{code: second_dispatch}} =
  Policy.dispatch(policy, run.decision.id, [now: 1_001, watermark: 1, state_revision: 1], fn -> raise "dispatched twice" end)

{:error, %LabError{code: ghost}} = Scenario.run(Keyword.put(run_opts, :actuator_id, "urn:wotex:lab:ghost"))

{:error, %LabError{code: stranger}} =
  Policy.decide(policy, run.action_proposal, principal: :stranger, watermark: 1, state_revision: 1, now: 5_000)

calls_before = Thing.stats(actuator).handler_calls

{:ok, granted} =
  Policy.decide(policy, run.action_proposal, principal: :operator, watermark: 9, state_revision: 1, now: 5_000, ttl: 100)

{:error, %LabError{code: stale}} =
  Policy.dispatch(policy, granted.id, [now: 5_001, watermark: 10, state_revision: 1], fn -> raise "stale" end)

{:error, %LabError{code: expired}} =
  Policy.dispatch(policy, granted.id, [now: 5_200, watermark: 9, state_revision: 1], fn -> raise "expired" end)

refusals = policy |> Policy.records() |> Map.fetch!(:refusals) |> Enum.map(& &1.reason)
{second_dispatch, ghost, stranger, stale, expired, Thing.stats(actuator).handler_calls == calls_before, refusals}
```

```elixir
:ok = Supervisor.stop(lab)
:ok = ThousandIsland.stop(server)
:ok = Agent.stop(clock)
:ok = Agent.stop(identifier)
if scripted?, do: Wotex.Lab.Test.MqttServer.stop(peer)
:ok
```

## Safe telemetry

The cycle emits runtime, HTTP, MQTT, directory, continuum, Nx and policy
spans. The dispatch span carries a non-reversible `thing_ref`, never the
Thing id; no reading, token, topic or URL becomes a label.

```elixir
drain = fn drain ->
  receive do
    {:wotex_lab_telemetry, event, measurements, metadata} ->
      [{event, measurements, metadata} | drain.(drain)]
  after
    0 -> []
  end
end

spans = drain.(drain)
:telemetry.detach(telemetry_id)

components = spans |> Enum.map(fn {[:wotex, :lab, component, _operation, _event], _m, _md} -> component end) |> Enum.uniq() |> Enum.sort()
dispatch_refs = for {[:wotex, :lab, :policy, :dispatch, :stop], _m, %{thing_ref: ref}} <- spans, do: ref
text = inspect(spans)

labels_safe? =
  dispatch_refs != [] and Enum.all?(dispatch_refs, &String.starts_with?(&1, "thing:")) and
    not (text =~ "urn:wotex") and not (text =~ token) and not (text =~ "21.5") and not (text =~ "127.0.0.1")

{components, labels_safe?}
```

## Expected output

| Check | Expectation |
| --- | --- |
| `things-discovered` | The thermostat and actuator (and the meter when present) are discovered by TD id |
| `proposal-in-limits` | `setTarget` with input about `22.5`, inside `[5, 35]` |
| `decision-granted` | The decision is granted and binds the proposal digest |
| `dispatched-once` | One `:accepted` dispatch; the actuator saw exactly two handler calls in the cycle |
| `effect-observed` | The actuator's `target` reads back as about `22.5` |
| `result-crossed-channel` | The cloud host received manifest, observation proposal and action result, in that order |
| `second-dispatch-refused` | `:already_dispatched`; ghost, stranger, stale and expired attempts dispatch nothing |
| `meter-lowers-target` (when a meter is present) | `2500` W over a `2000` W budget gives `20.5`; a `3000` W budget gives `22.5` |

```elixir
close? = fn left, right -> abs(left - right) < 0.0001 end
expected_things = if meter_td, do: 3, else: 2

base = %{
  "things-discovered" =>
    map_size(things) == expected_things and Map.has_key?(things, ThingDescription.id(actuator_td)) and
      Map.has_key?(things, ThingDescription.id(thermostat_td)),
  "proposal-in-limits" => proposal_fields.action_name == "setTarget" and close?.(proposal_fields.input, 22.5),
  "decision-granted" =>
    run.decision.status == :granted and run.decision.proposal_digest == Policy.proposal_digest(run.action_proposal),
  "dispatched-once" => dispatch_status == :accepted and actuator_after_run.handler_calls == 2,
  "effect-observed" => close?.(run.effect, 22.5),
  "result-crossed-channel" =>
    Enum.map(stats.received, & &1.kind) == ["continuum_manifest", "observation_proposal", "action_result"],
  "second-dispatch-refused" =>
    second_dispatch == :already_dispatched and ghost == :thing_not_discovered and stranger == :principal_denied and
      stale == :stale_observation and expired == :expired and labels_safe?
}

meter = %{
  "meter-lowers-target" =>
    match?(%{power: 2500, over_effect: over, under_effect: under} when abs(over - 20.5) < 0.0001 and abs(under - 22.5) < 0.0001, meter_runs)
}

if meter_td, do: Map.merge(base, meter), else: base
```

## Public seam

Every consumer-implements seam at once: `runtime.transport` (loopback),
`runtime.credentials` (`StaticRef`), `http.client` (`ReqClient`),
`mqtt.client` (`EmqttClient`), `directory.repository` (`EtsRepository`),
`directory.authorization`, `directory.clock`, `directory.identifier`, and
the Lab-owned `lab.policy` and `lab.continuum_channel`.

## Spec and completion IDs

* Lab: WLB.03, WLB.04, WLB.05, WLB.06 (`WLB-C06`, `WLB-C08`).
* Upstream: consumer evidence only through the seams above; no upstream
  completion item is claimed by this notebook.

## Replacement adapter

Swap any adapter named in the seam list without touching the scenario:
`Scenario.discover/3` takes the profiles, transports and credential port
you pass; `Scenario.run/1` takes the channel, host endpoint names and policy
you started. Replacing the policy means implementing grant, dispatch-once
and revoke with the same binding fields (digest, principal, watermark,
revision, expiry); a policy that dispatches on a bare proposal is not a
replacement, it is a removal of the authority boundary.
